    {
      "dom_id": "question-84440",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14200038/assets/5245725446c23cc37e5ca4ad5b4def939c1544100eb3488092f59c4ed0f8beaa.png)\n\nConsider the sample space $S$ with the Venn diagram given above. What is $P(A)?$",
      "worked_solution": "From the given Venn diagram, we have $P(A)=y$ and $P({A}^{′})=\\frac{y}{22}.$\nTherefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A)+P({A}^{′}) & =1 \\\\ y+\\frac{y}{22} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{23y}{22} & =1 \\\\ y & =\\frac{22}{23}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently,  $P(A)=y=\\frac{22}{23}.$",
